Do not define PROTOBUF_DESCRIPTOR_WEAK_MESSAGES_ALLOWED on Windows

protobuf 29.5 turns weak descriptor messages on for every clang that is
not Apple's or MSVC's, which includes clang (zig) targeting MinGW. Its
InitWeakDefaults then needs the ELF linker's __start_pb_defaults and
__stop_pb_defaults section symbols, which COFF linkers (lld-link) do not
provide: protoc.exe and every program linking libprotobuf.a fail with
"undefined symbol: __start_pb_defaults". Upstream's fix, backported
unchanged: protocolbuffers/protobuf commit 5769732ec0 ("Fix linker
errors on Windows with clang", #20025, fixes #16844), in v31.0. The
header is installed, so code compiled against the package sees the same
guard.

--- a/src/google/protobuf/port_def.inc
+++ b/src/google/protobuf/port_def.inc
@@ -652,7 +652,7 @@
 #error PROTOBUF_DESCRIPTOR_WEAK_MESSAGES_ALLOWED was previously defined
 #endif
 #if defined(__GNUC__) && defined(__clang__) && !defined(__APPLE__) && \
-    !defined(_MSC_VER)
+    !defined(_MSC_VER) && !defined(_WIN32)
 #define PROTOBUF_DESCRIPTOR_WEAK_MESSAGES_ALLOWED
 #endif
 
